# wiki/gaps.md is an append-mostly list that nearly every PR adds a section
# to, so concurrent PRs conflict on it constantly (13 of 20 recent main
# commits touched it). Git's built-in union driver keeps both sides of a
# conflicting hunk, which is the correct resolution for independent gap
# entries. It applies to local merges and rebases (Hive's review-stage
# rebase, operator `git merge origin/main`); GitHub's own mergeability check
# ignores merge drivers, so a PR still shows a conflict until it is merged
# locally. Review the result for duplicated lines when both sides edited the
# same entry.
wiki/gaps.md merge=union
